  "//peerDependencies": [
    "Everything here is optional: Bali is a component library and no app uses all of it.",
    "Block Editor (subpath ./block-editor): @blocknote/core + /react + /mantine, @mantine/core,",
    "  @mantine/hooks, react, react-dom -- all MPL-2.0 or MIT. `shiki` is only needed for",
    "  syntax-highlighted code blocks; pass syntax_highlighting: false and you can skip it.",
    "Rich Text Editor (subpath ./rich-text-editor): the @tiptap/* set plus lowlight, highlight.js,",
    "  tippy.js and lodash.throttle. This list previously existed only as a code comment that",
    "  named three packages and trailed off in an ellipsis.",
    "DELIBERATELY ABSENT -- @blocknote/xl-ai, xl-multi-column, xl-pdf-exporter, xl-docx-exporter",
    "  and their companions (`ai`, `docx`, `@react-pdf/renderer`). Those four are",
    "  'GPL-3.0 OR PROPRIETARY': a closed-source application needs a paid commercial licence.",
    "  Declaring them as peers led people to install them by reflex. They are documented in",
    "  docs/api/block-editor.md, and the loader keeps them lazy so an app that never turns those",
    "  features on still builds and runs without them."
  ],
